    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d83">

                <pb facs="0119" n="109" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg109"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00115 European War 1939/7558: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harrison</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bern</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-29T17:00:00+01:00">October 29, 1943—5
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 7:37 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>6769. American interests, Germany. Your 2366, September 27.<anchor n="42"
                        xml:id="d83-f1"/> Foreign Office official informally gave Tait<anchor n="43"
                        xml:id="d83-f2"/> following received from <pb facs="0120" n="110"
                        xml:id="pg110"/> Secretary Soldati, Swiss Legation, Berlin, by telephone
                    October 27, which is considered sufficiently important immediate communication
                    to the Department.</p>
                <p>Germans attach great importance in possible exchange to 37 individuals mentioned
                    in second paragraph of your 2366. Soldati believes, if possible, include these
                    persons in exchange will greatly facilitate satisfactory conclusion exchange
                    negotiations.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harrison</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
